  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "performance",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "Several collection operations scanned every tensor name to select an exact prefix and its dot-separated descendants.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_b2c1b1b37440485bb48f0e0c63ea07e4"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "Caching a tensor-name trie appears intended to reduce repeated prefix-search work. The source establishes the mechanism, not a measured performance improvement.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_27fb6264a2d54ac88cdac7ff6197a9a8"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "Both dependency declarations add marisa_trie, matching the helper's local import. A whole-parent-tree search for marisa found no existing occurrence; dynamic and external imports remain outside that result.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_3c9e21f6d2a0454893befc1edf6d2703",
          "call_fadf4be3ba6b40a69aaf8aecba19caba",
          "call_4a67ab37dc4d4a21bfeb3e05e092b6af",
          "call_27fb6264a2d54ac88cdac7ff6197a9a8"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "The root loading-tokenization entry establishes the original exact-or-dot-descendant contract. The tensor-override entry establishes main-based enumeration and wildcard source routing, and records inherited metrics incompatibilities.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_00d8de693314412ba20b77171595a5d7",
          "call_3de2ee97a354494fb955e3787e257e96"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #33, \u201cError converting model,\u201d reports a file-opening failure through compile_model, get_tensors and get_tensor. Its connection to this change is inference from matching functions, not evidence that trie indexing fixes that failure. Issue #38, \u201cError converting nvidia/Llama-3_1-Nemotron-Ultra-253B-v1,\u201d instead concerns tensor padding.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_a68cb7aa0fa843939d90a068fb026a88",
          "call_797f3df9c17b4f3c842434bf56e363b1",
          "call_9a0ec88af1cf40eca54c290b68da2898",
          "call_27fb6264a2d54ac88cdac7ff6197a9a8"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "No repository loader, marisa_trie implementation, checkpoint I/O or GPU code was executed. The Python check transcribed selection logic and modeled a cached snapshot.",
      "Trie ordering, construction cost, memory use and measured search improvement remain unverified.",
      "Literal caller searches do not establish external compatibility. No inspected checkpoint demonstrates an exact-prefix collision in a shipped workflow.",
      "Only opening portions of discussions #7, #26, #33, #34, #42, #48, #52, #53, #55 and #58 were inspected; those reads do not establish this change's motivation."
    ],
    "links": [
      "543c4b27714c6a677a6e714c452d62532f634cff",
      "6341b119efc4ef73ff2e4adcdd14a4d79b0a5e6d"
    ],
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "loading",
        "title": "Cached tensor-name prefix indexing",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "get_tensor_file_map_trie imports marisa_trie on demand and constructs Trie(self.tensor_file_map.keys()), retaining the result with lru_cache. The trie indexes names; filenames and metadata remain in the existing dictionaries.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_27fb6264a2d54ac88cdac7ff6197a9a8",
              "call_b2c1b1b37440485bb48f0e0c63ea07e4"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Ordinary list_tensors and get_tensors, plus variant get_tensor_sizes and list_tensors, now query trie.keys(prefix + '.'). Ordinary get_tensor_sizes and variant get_tensors retain their full scans. Thus the change does not uniformly replace every prefix selector.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_27fb6264a2d54ac88cdac7ff6197a9a8",
              "call_b2c1b1b37440485bb48f0e0c63ea07e4"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Variant queries still enumerate main's namespace and resolve each selected name through find_stc; replacement-only names remain outside bulk enumeration. The added ordinary find_stc returns self. Parent-tree find_stc references were confined to the variant implementation and supplied tensor-name strings.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_27fb6264a2d54ac88cdac7ff6197a9a8",
              "call_b2c1b1b37440485bb48f0e0c63ea07e4",
              "call_eff620e53b4e41da937e54b6c7708898"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "compile_model obtains module sizes before reading each module's tensors through get_tensors(prefix, allow_bf16=True). Model.get_storage_info uses get_tensor_sizes for unloaded modules. These consumers retain string module prefixes and do not compensate for the changed selectors.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9a0ec88af1cf40eca54c290b68da2898",
              "call_cbc0c84b251246889f6f7539a598b56d",
              "call_27fb6264a2d54ac88cdac7ff6197a9a8"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The retained index introduces a coherence requirement because add_tensor_files can mutate the name map. Keeping live scans avoids that requirement; using a cached trie requires invalidation or an immutable-map contract, neither supplied by this diff.",
            "basis": "inference",
            "evidence": [
              "call_b2c1b1b37440485bb48f0e0c63ea07e4",
              "call_27fb6264a2d54ac88cdac7ff6197a9a8"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A Python transcription selected a filename for an exact tensor prefix and raised KeyError when using it as a tensor-map key. A separate cached-snapshot model omitted a newly added descendant that live-map enumeration included.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_ed46dd336dbc40e78f854f595458e2c8"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The inherited metrics incompatibilities are carried over: the variant constructor initializes only main and stcs, shared initialization accesses config.stc.metrics, and Model.get_load_metrics calls get_metrics, which neither collection defines. The task diff does not change these interfaces.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_b2c1b1b37440485bb48f0e0c63ea07e4",
              "call_1c831e16b2714f0cbfe475066dcfb4cc",
              "call_cbc0c84b251246889f6f7539a598b56d",
              "call_27fb6264a2d54ac88cdac7ff6197a9a8"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
